  <section id="top" class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pete Guzzo</p>
        <h1 class="display">Twenty years of production. <span class="accent">A system of AI agents</span> built to run the other half of it.</h1>
        <p class="sub">Take complicated work and make it land with a real audience, without losing what made it true in the first place. Technical work. Creative work. Operational work. That's been the craft for twenty years. For the last several months, it's also been an architecture I designed, built, and ran myself: CORTEX.</p>
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <div><p class="k">Production</p><p class="v">20+ years, film / TV / broadcast</p></div>
          <div><p class="k">Current base</p><p class="v">Shear Media Studios, St. Petersburg FL</p></div>
          <div><p class="k">System</p><p class="v">CORTEX. Running, not conceptual.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-photo"><img src="/images/about/pete-on-set-shear.jpg" alt="Pete Guzzo on set at Shear Media Studios" /></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section id="cortex" class="bordered"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">What CORTEX is</p>
    <h2 class="display">My AI architecture, not a single tool.</h2>
    <p class="lede">CORTEX is the operating system I built and run underneath everything on this page. It's not one assistant. It's a team of named AI agents, each with one defined job, a supervisory layer that coordinates them, and a memory that persists across sessions instead of resetting every time. One rule never moves: nothing publishes, ships, or spends under my name without me checking it first.</p>
    <p class="prose">Two decks run inside it at the same time: the physical production side and the AI system side. They're not separate projects. They feed each other.</p>
    <div class="decks" style="margin-top:8px;">
      <div class="deck">
        <p class="tag">The physical side</p>
        <h3>Production</h3>
        <p>Two decades directing and producing film, documentary, television, national advertising, nonprofit and branded content, including award-winning work recognized nationally.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Built and run Shear Media Studios, about 15,000 sq ft, in St. Petersburg, FL</li>
          <li>Closed and run the Barstool Sports contract, a recurring weekly live broadcast, sold on the strength of the studio</li>
          <li>Developed 211 Studio, Channelside, now home to the episodic series <em>A Land Remembered</em></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="deck">
        <p class="tag">The system side</p>
        <h3>CORTEX</h3>
        <p>An operational intelligence system built around named AI agents with defined roles, a supervisory layer, and a human approval gate that doesn't move. Nothing ships without me.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>This site was built by the system it describes. See the full build chain.</li>
          <li>Verified-claims discipline: no fact enters copy without a traceable source</li>
          <li>Memory that persists across sessions instead of resetting every time</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

