  <section id="verse" class="bordered"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Inside CORTEX</p>
    <h2 class="display">The Verse: what's actually running in post.</h2>
    <p class="lede">I didn't build this to replace an editor. I built it because an editor today already has five jobs.</p>

    <p class="prose">Organize the footage. Run the renders. Do a first audio pass before it even gets anywhere near a mixer. Cut the story. Repackage it for three different screen shapes. One person doing all of that needs an assistant. That's what the Verse is: an assistant, not a replacement.</p>

    <p class="prose">Everything it automates is work I was already going to do myself, just slower. It's 100% my ingenuity in there. My flow. My way of editing. The Verse doesn't decide what the story is. I do.</p>

    <p class="prose">Here's the part that actually matters: it isn't one AI agent trying to do all of it, or even two or three. The work is split up the same way you'd split it among a real human crew. One person indexing footage isn't the same person mixing audio, and the person mixing audio isn't the same person doing color. Each job gets its own specialist.</p>

    <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Seven roles, not one agent doing everything</p>

